id: 22
hanzi: 球迷
pinyin: qiú mí
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Noun

meanings_summary:
  en: ball game fan; soccer/basketball enthusiast
  es: aficionado al fútbol/baloncesto; fanático de la pelota

senses[1]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Noun | Standard | a passionate enthusiast and supporter of ball sports such as football, basketball, or tennis | persona apasionada seguidora de deportes de pelota como fútbol o baloncesto | 狂热的足球迷 (a fanatical soccer fan)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 当主队在补时阶段攻入绝杀进球时，看台上数万名狂热的球迷激动得热泪盈眶并高声欢呼。 | Dāng zhǔduì zài bǔshí jiēduàn gōngrù juéshā jìnqiú shí, kàntái shang shùwàn míng kuángrè de qiúmí jīdòng de rèlèi-yíngkuàng bìng gāoshēng huānhū. | When the home team netted the buzzer-beating winning goal in stoppage time, tens of thousands of fervent fans on the stands cheered with tears in their eyes. | Al anotar el equipo local el gol del triunfo en el descuento, decenas de miles de hinchas en las gradas rompieron a llorar de emoción y a vitorear.
  #2 | 虽然今晚下着滂沱大雨，但依然有许多忠实球迷早早守候在体育馆外等待与球星签名合影。 | Suīrán jīnwǎn xià zhe pángtuó dàyǔ, dàn yīrán yǒu xǔduō zhōngshí qiúmí zǎozǎo shǒuhòu zài tǐyùguǎn wài děngdài yǔ qiúxīng qiānmíng héyǐng. | Despite pouring rain tonight, many devoted fans waited outside the arena early for autographs and photos with sports stars. | Pese al diluvio de esta noche, numerosos aficionados leales aguardaron ante el pabellón para conseguir autógrafos de sus ídolos.

collocations[6]{hanzi,en}:
  忠实球迷 | loyal ball fan
  狂热球迷 | fanatical enthusiast
  资深球迷 | veteran sports fan
  篮球迷 | basketball fan
  足球迷 | soccer fan
  球迷见面会 | fan meet-and-greet event

idioms[4]{hanzi,pinyin,meaning_en}:
  如醉如痴 | rú zuì rú chī | entranced and infatuated; utterly spellbound
  万人空巷 | wàn rén kōng xiàng | the whole town empties out to celebrate an event
  助威呐喊 | zhù wēi nà hǎn | shout encouragement and cheer loudly
  热火朝天 | rè huǒ cháo tiān | seething with fiery enthusiasm; buzzing activity

character_decomposition[2]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  球 | qiú | ball; sphere; globe; orb | pelota; balón; esfera; globo | 王 | jade / king | 王 (jade stone / precious gem) + 求 (fur coat / curling) | 求 (qiú / phonetic) | 11 | 左右结构 | Jade radical 王 beside 求; originally a fine round jade sphere, extended to modern sports spheres and balls. | A precious polished jade sphere (王) bouncing smoothly like a ball (球). | Una preciosa piedra de jade pulida en esfera redonda (王) que bota como una pelota (球). | 35 | MGIJE | 球
  迷 | mí | fan; enthusiast; enchant; lost | aficionado; cautivado; perderse | 辶 | movement | 辶 (wandering movement) + 米 (dispersed grains) | 米 (mǐ / phonetic association) | 9 | 半包围结构 | Movement radical 辶 with scattered grain 米; wandering captivated in confusing paths, extended to passionate obsession. | Following scattered trails of rice grains (米) along winding paths (辶) in passionate fascination (迷). | Seguir senderos de granos de arroz (米) absorto en el camino (辶) entregado a la pasión (迷). | 35 | YFD | 迷

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: One who is utterly fascinated (迷) by the bouncing ball (球) is a true sports fan (球迷).
  composite_memory_hook_es: Quien se siente cautivado (迷) por el movimiento del balón (球) es un verdadero aficionado (球迷).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: The suffix '迷' denotes avid passion or enthusiasts (歌迷 fan of singing, 影迷 movie buff, 球迷 sports fan).
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: Two rising second tones: 'qiú mí' (35-35). Both rise in pitch with smooth vocal energy.

traps_and_cognates:
  look_alikes[4]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,distinction_note}:
    球 | qiú | ball; globe | Jade radical 王 on left with 求
    救 | jiù | rescue; save | Has 求 on left with 攵 (tap) on right
    迷 | mí | fan; lost | Movement radical 辶 at bottom of 米
    谜 | mí | riddle; puzzle | Speech radical 讠 on left of 迷
  etymological_cognates[4]{character,pinyin,gloss_en}:
    粉 | fěn | powder; fan (slang)
    友 | yǒu | friend; companion
    众 | zhòng | crowd; spectators
    徒 | tú | disciple; follower

semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 球迷 specifically designates dedicated fans or followers of ball-related athletic sports.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 球迷 vs. 观众 | guānzhòng | 观众 refers broadly to any passive audience member watching a show, whereas 球迷 implies emotional attachment to a ball club.
    2 | 球迷 vs. 粉丝 | fěnsī | 粉丝 is a generic modern umbrella term for celebrity/pop fans, while 球迷 is specialized for sporting ball events.
    3 | 球迷 vs. 队员 | duìyuán | 队员 is an active roster athlete playing on the court, while 球迷 supports from the bleachers.

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 看台上的球迷是球场上无可争议的第十二人。无论是在球队遭遇连败的至暗低谷，还是在问鼎冠军的荣耀时刻，那面迎风飘扬的俱乐部巨幅旗帜下，始终汇聚着最执着真诚的掌声与最滚烫炽热的呐喊。 | Kàntái shang de qiúmí shì qiúchǎng shang wúkě-zhēngyì de dì-shí'èr rén. Wúlùn shì zài qiúduì zāoyù liánbài de zhì'àn dīgǔ, háishì zài wèndǐng guànjūn de róngyào shíkè, nà miàn yíngfēng piāoyáng de jùlébù jùfú qízhì xià, shǐzhōng huìjù zhe zuì zhízhuó zhēnchéng de zhǎngshēng yǔ zuì gǔntàng chìrè de nàhǎn. | Fans in the stands are indisputably the team's twelfth player. Whether during dark losing streaks or crowning championship glory, under the massive fluttering club banner gathers the most devoted applause and fiery roar. | La hinchada en la grada es el jugador número doce. Tanto en las derrotas más dolorosas como al alzar el trofeo, bajo la ondeante pancarta del club resuenan siempre los aplausos más leales y los cánticos más fervorosos.
  #2 | 早年在春田学院，看台上坐满了年轻球迷。每当有人投篮入筐，大家刚想喝彩，比赛却因慢吞吞搬梯取球而叫停。为了不辜负球迷的观赛热情，工匠毅然用锯子开掉筐底，赋予了篮球运动极其流畅的竞技节奏。 | Zǎonián zài Chūntián xuéyuàn, kàntái shang zuòmǎn le niánqīng qiúmí. Měidāng yǒurén tóulán rù kuāng, dàjiā gāng xiǎng hècǎi, bǐsài què yīn màntūntūn bān tī qǔ qiú ér jiàotíng. Wèile bù gūfù qiúmí de guānsài rèqíng, gōngjiàng yìrán yòng jùzi kāi diào kuāngdǐ, fùyǔ le lánqiú yùndòng jíqí liúchàng de jìngjì jiézòu. | At Springfield College, stands were filled with young fans. Whenever a basket was scored, play was halted while ladders were dragged out. To satisfy fan passion, craftsmen sawed off the bottoms, gifting basketball a delightfully fluid rhythm. | En Springfield, las gradas rebosaban de jóvenes hinchas. Al encestar, el juego paraba para traer la escalera. Para no defraudar a la afición, los conserjes serraron el fondo, dotando al baloncesto de un ritmo trepidante.
